### What changed:
1. **Timestamp Fallback for `SUPERSEDED`:** In Step 5, if both rows in a comparison have valid timestamps, it compares `tsMs` (and breaks ties with `rawIndex`). If either row has an unparseable/missing timestamp (`tsMs === null`), it falls back to `other.rawIndex < item.rawIndex` so the top-most row in the sheet is kept and subsequent ones are marked `SUPERSEDED`.
2. **`Review_Reasons` (Column Q):** Collects any triggered checks in order (`YN`, `Phone`, `MissingTimestamp`, `Park`, `DUP-email`, `DUP-name-time`) and joins them into a comma-separated string right next to `Review_Status`. Rows with `OK` status leave this cell blank.

