The key change is in the percent-formatting step. Instead of formatting the entire percent column in one call (which would format blank cells too), it now loops through each cell in each percent column and applies `0.0%` only when the cell's value is not empty. This is slightly slower on very large sheets but ensures blank cells stay truly blank with no visible formatting artifact.

